00:47:19.780 --> 00:47:21.780
Our behavior was

cue0148487
00:47:21.780 --> 00:47:23.780
heroic.

cue0148488
00:47:23.780 --> 00:47:25.780
And yet, apparently,

cue0148489
00:47:25.780 --> 00:47:27.780
Borea ʿOlam

cue0148490
00:47:27.780 --> 00:47:29.780
did not respond

cue0148491
00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:31.780
to our needs.

cue0148492
00:47:31.780 --> 00:47:33.780
That was one thing.

cue0148493
00:47:33.780 --> 00:47:35.780
At the same time,

cue0148494
00:47:35.780 --> 00:47:37.780
around, maybe

cue0148495
00:47:37.780 --> 00:47:39.780
off for a few years,

cue0148496
00:47:39.780 --> 00:47:41.780
maybe, around the year, no, what should I be

cue0148497
00:47:41.780 --> 00:47:43.780
off for a few years, I don't know exactly,

cue0148498
00:47:43.780 --> 00:47:45.780
around the year 1640,

cue0148499
00:47:45.780 --> 00:47:47.780
but I may be off

cue0148500
00:47:47.780 --> 00:47:49.780
by a few years,

cue0148501
00:47:49.780 --> 00:47:51.780
1640, no, I'm sorry,

cue0148502
00:47:51.780 --> 00:47:53.780
yes, 1640, 1646,

cue0148503
00:47:53.780 --> 00:47:55.780
pogroms

cue0148504
00:47:55.780 --> 00:47:57.780
start spreading through Europe.

cue0148505
00:47:57.780 --> 00:47:59.780
Russia,

cue0148506
00:47:59.780 --> 00:48:01.780
Russian Jewry,

cue0148507
00:48:01.780 --> 00:48:03.780
and Polish Jewry

cue0148508
00:48:03.780 --> 00:48:05.780
are being devastated by

cue0148509
00:48:05.780 --> 00:48:07.780
the Cossacks, by the Czars,

cue0148510
00:48:07.780 --> 00:48:09.780
and so on.

cue0148511
00:48:09.780 --> 00:48:11.780
And at the time, therefore, all of a sudden,

cue0148512
00:48:11.780 --> 00:48:13.780
we find ourselves

cue0148513
00:48:13.780 --> 00:48:15.780
beleaguered,

cue0148514
00:48:15.780 --> 00:48:17.780
both in the Sepharadi communities

cue0148515
00:48:17.780 --> 00:48:19.780
and the ʾAshkenaz communities.

cue0148516
00:48:19.780 --> 00:48:21.780
And scores

cue0148517
00:48:21.780 --> 00:48:23.780
of ʾAshkenaz refugees,

cue0148518
00:48:23.780 --> 00:48:25.780
yes,

cue0148519
00:48:25.780 --> 00:48:27.780
from Poland, mainly from Poland,

cue0148520
00:48:27.780 --> 00:48:29.780
and Ukraine, and so on,

cue0148521
00:48:29.780 --> 00:48:31.780
pour into Turkey.

cue0148522
00:48:31.780 --> 00:48:33.780
And all of a sudden, the Sepharadim discover

cue0148523
00:48:33.780 --> 00:48:35.780
the atrocities

cue0148524
00:48:35.780 --> 00:48:37.780
committed against

cue0148525
00:48:37.780 --> 00:48:39.780
Jews in ʾAshkenaz countries.

cue0148526
00:48:39.780 --> 00:48:41.780
And we were

cue0148527
00:48:41.780 --> 00:48:43.780
angry again, angry.

cue0148528
00:48:43.780 --> 00:48:45.780
The Messiah should have come.

cue0148529
00:48:45.780 --> 00:48:47.780
Alright, fine.

cue0148530
00:48:47.780 --> 00:48:49.780
So here I'm telling you

cue0148531
00:48:49.780 --> 00:48:51.780
the historical things.

cue0148532
00:48:51.780 --> 00:48:53.780
But something else also happened.

cue0148533
00:48:55.780 --> 00:48:57.780
In the time of Maran,

cue0148534
00:48:57.780 --> 00:48:59.780
while Maran was alive,

cue0148535
00:48:59.780 --> 00:49:01.780
the greatest

cue0148536
00:49:01.780 --> 00:49:03.780
mekubal was the Talmud

cue0148537
00:49:03.780 --> 00:49:05.780
of Maran.

cue0148538
00:49:05.780 --> 00:49:07.780
Rabbeinu Moshe Cordobeinu. He was considered

cue0148539
00:49:07.780 --> 00:49:09.780
the greatest Kabbalist.

cue0148540
00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:11.780
In the time of Maran, you say,

cue0148541
00:49:11.780 --> 00:49:13.780
Moshe Cordobeinu must have died around

cue0148542
00:49:13.780 --> 00:49:15.780
when he was a junior to Maran.

cue0148543
00:49:15.780 --> 00:49:17.780
He must have died about the year 1576.

cue0148544
00:49:17.780 --> 00:49:19.780
More or less. I could be off

cue0148545
00:49:19.780 --> 00:49:21.780
a few years there.

cue0148546
00:49:21.780 --> 00:49:23.780
He was considered the greatest mekubal.

cue0148547
00:49:23.780 --> 00:49:25.780
Alright.

cue0148548
00:49:25.780 --> 00:49:27.780
But then, there was a young man

cue0148549
00:49:27.780 --> 00:49:29.780
who nobody

cue0148550
00:49:29.780 --> 00:49:31.780
actually knew. I mean, they knew

cue0148551
00:49:31.780 --> 00:49:33.780
that that's a brilliant man

cue0148552
00:49:33.780 --> 00:49:35.780
in his 30s. He died in his 30s.

cue0148553
00:49:35.780 --> 00:49:37.780
And that was the famous Ha'ari.

cue0148554
00:49:39.780 --> 00:49:41.780
Ha'ari

cue0148555
00:49:41.780 --> 00:49:43.780
was an extraordinary human being.

cue0148556
00:49:43.780 --> 00:49:45.780
First of all, he was a great posek.

cue0148557
00:49:45.780 --> 00:49:47.780
He knew halakha very well.

cue0148558
00:49:47.780 --> 00:49:49.780
He was born in Egypt

cue0148559
00:49:49.780 --> 00:49:51.780
and he was a student for a while

cue0148560
00:49:51.780 --> 00:49:53.780
of the Radvaz.

cue0148561
00:49:53.780 --> 00:49:55.780
He was a junior in age because he died.

cue0148562
00:49:55.780 --> 00:49:57.780
He died at the age of 32, 33.

cue0148563
00:49:57.780 --> 00:49:59.780
He was a businessman

cue0148564
00:49:59.780 --> 00:50:01.780
and he was a posek.

cue0148565
00:50:01.780 --> 00:50:03.780
He was a dayan. In some pesakim,

cue0148566
00:50:03.780 --> 00:50:05.780
he signed as a dayan.

cue0148567
00:50:05.780 --> 00:50:07.780
And he comes then to

cue0148568
00:50:07.780 --> 00:50:09.780
ʾEreṣ Yiśraʾel, to Safed.

cue0148569
00:50:09.780 --> 00:50:11.780
And there he has a small

cue0148570
00:50:11.780 --> 00:50:13.780
school for mekubalim.

cue0148571
00:50:13.780 --> 00:50:15.780
He did not write anything on qabbala.

cue0148572
00:50:15.780 --> 00:50:17.780
Not one line.

cue0148573
00:50:17.780 --> 00:50:19.780
But he produced

cue0148574
00:50:19.780 --> 00:50:21.780
many, not many, a few talmidim.

cue0148575
00:50:21.780 --> 00:50:23.780
The greatest

cue0148576
00:50:23.780 --> 00:50:25.780
was Moharachu Rabbeinu Chaim

cue0148577
00:50:25.780 --> 00:50:27.780
Vital.

cue0148578
00:50:27.780 --> 00:50:29.780
Rabbeinu Chaim Vital

cue0148579
00:50:29.780 --> 00:50:31.780
eventually goes to Damascus

cue0148580
00:50:31.780 --> 00:50:33.780
and he is a dayan because his

cue0148581
00:50:33.780 --> 00:50:35.780
last name is

cue0148582
00:50:35.780 --> 00:50:37.780
Moharachu Chaim.

cue0148583
00:50:37.780 --> 00:50:39.780
Vital is the Italian for

cue0148584
00:50:39.780 --> 00:50:41.780
Chaim. And his last name

cue0148585
00:50:41.780 --> 00:50:43.780
well you won't believe it.

cue0148586
00:50:43.780 --> 00:50:45.780
Calabrese.

cue0148587
00:50:45.780 --> 00:50:47.780
Rabbeinu Chaim Vital Calabrese.

cue0148588
00:50:47.780 --> 00:50:49.780
He was from Calabria.

cue0148589
00:50:49.780 --> 00:50:51.780
From Sicily. He was from

cue0148590
00:50:51.780 --> 00:50:53.780
Gerush Sicilia. Sicily.

cue0148591
00:50:53.780 --> 00:50:55.780
And in Damascus they had

cue0148592
00:50:55.780 --> 00:50:57.780
the Gerush Sicilia went to Damascus.

cue0148593
00:50:57.780 --> 00:50:59.780
And he became the dayan in

cue0148594
00:50:59.780 --> 00:51:01.780
the Gerush Sicilia, in the Sicilian community

cue0148595
00:51:01.780 --> 00:51:03.780
in Damascus.

cue0148596
00:51:03.780 --> 00:51:05.780
He was the great mekubal, the talmid of Ha'ari.

cue0148597
00:51:05.780 --> 00:51:07.780
What this has to do with us?

cue0148598
00:51:07.780 --> 00:51:09.780
A lot.

cue0148599
00:51:09.780 --> 00:51:11.780
Because Ha'ari believed

cue0148600
00:51:11.780 --> 00:51:13.780
that the reason

cue0148601
00:51:13.780 --> 00:51:15.780
why the Mashiaḥ doesn't come

cue0148602
00:51:15.780 --> 00:51:17.780
is because of certain sins,

cue0148603
00:51:17.780 --> 00:51:19.780
of certain

cue0148604
00:51:19.780 --> 00:51:21.780
flaws in the personality,

cue0148605
00:51:21.780 --> 00:51:23.780
in the prayers,

cue0148606
00:51:23.780 --> 00:51:25.780
in the liturgy of the Jews.

cue0148607
00:51:25.780 --> 00:51:27.780
Kabbanot and so on.

cue0148608
00:51:27.780 --> 00:51:29.780
And that was the

cue0148609
00:51:29.780 --> 00:51:31.780
theory. You want to see

cue0148610
00:51:31.780 --> 00:51:33.780
how this affected

cue0148611
00:51:33.780 --> 00:51:35.780
history.

cue0148612
00:51:35.780 --> 00:51:37.780
Fine. This is

cue0148613
00:51:37.780 --> 00:51:39.780
the background. Three things.

cue0148614
00:51:39.780 --> 00:51:41.780
Suffering of the

cue0148615
00:51:41.780 --> 00:51:43.780
Sepharadim. Suffering

cue0148616
00:51:43.780 --> 00:51:45.780
of the ʾAshkenazim.

cue0148617
00:51:45.780 --> 00:51:47.780
In a theory that tells you the Mashiaḥ

cue0148618
00:51:47.780 --> 00:51:49.780
depends

cue0148619
00:51:49.780 --> 00:51:51.780
on certain mystical

cue0148620
00:51:51.780 --> 00:51:53.780
ideology or ideas

cue0148621
00:51:53.780 --> 00:51:55.780
that should be implemented.

cue0148622
00:51:55.780 --> 00:51:57.780
These are the three ingredients.

cue0148623
00:51:57.780 --> 00:51:59.780
Now.

cue0148624
00:51:59.780 --> 00:52:01.780
Forget now about what I said.

cue0148625
00:52:01.780 --> 00:52:03.780
Leave this into your background.

cue0148626
00:52:03.780 --> 00:52:05.780
And you're going to go into one of the most

cue0148627
00:52:05.780 --> 00:52:07.780
fantastic stories.

cue0148628
00:52:07.780 --> 00:52:09.780
And I'm saying this with seriousness.

cue0148629
00:52:09.780 --> 00:52:11.780
I do regret

cue0148630
00:52:11.780 --> 00:52:13.780
that I have no musical talents.

cue0148631
00:52:13.780 --> 00:52:15.780
If I would have musical talents,

cue0148632
00:52:15.780 --> 00:52:17.780
I would write,

cue0148633
00:52:17.780 --> 00:52:19.780
I don't say it has to make fun of anybody,

cue0148634
00:52:19.780 --> 00:52:21.780
I would write either an opera

cue0148635
00:52:21.780 --> 00:52:23.780
or a great

cue0148636
00:52:23.780 --> 00:52:25.780
musical for

cue0148637
00:52:25.780 --> 00:52:27.780
the story of Shabbat HaSevi.

cue0148638
00:52:27.780 --> 00:52:29.780
Because it deserves it. It's an extraordinary

cue0148639
00:52:29.780 --> 00:52:31.780
extraordinary story.

cue0148640
00:52:31.780 --> 00:52:33.780
Now.

cue0148641
00:52:35.780 --> 00:52:37.780
Shabbat HaSevi was born in

cue0148642
00:52:37.780 --> 00:52:39.780
Izmirna

cue0148643
00:52:39.780 --> 00:52:41.780
1626.

cue0148644
00:52:41.780 --> 00:52:43.780
And he died in

cue0148645
00:52:43.780 --> 00:52:45.780
what is today Albania

cue0148646
00:52:45.780 --> 00:52:47.780
1676.

cue0148647
00:52:47.780 --> 00:52:49.780
He lived exactly 50 years.

cue0148648
00:52:49.780 --> 00:52:51.780
His parents

cue0148649
00:52:51.780 --> 00:52:53.780
came from

cue0148650
00:52:53.780 --> 00:52:55.780
the Greek islands. The islands where they spoke

cue0148651
00:52:55.780 --> 00:52:57.780
Greek.

cue0148652
00:52:57.780 --> 00:52:59.780
Probably, we don't know for sure,

cue0148653
00:52:59.780 --> 00:53:01.780
the parents were ʾAshkenazim.

cue0148654
00:53:01.780 --> 00:53:03.780
But it's not sure. This is

cue0148655
00:53:03.780 --> 00:53:05.780
speculation among scholars.

cue0148656
00:53:05.780 --> 00:53:07.780
But it certainly was not Sepharadim.

cue0148657
00:53:07.780 --> 00:53:09.780
He didn't come from the Spanish speaking

cue0148658
00:53:09.780 --> 00:53:11.780
communities. He came from a community

cue0148659
00:53:11.780 --> 00:53:13.780
from an island that were like

cue0148660
00:53:13.780 --> 00:53:15.780
ʾAshkenazim and so on, that were Greek

cue0148661
00:53:15.780 --> 00:53:17.780
speaking communities.

cue0148662
00:53:17.780 --> 00:53:19.780
But, so it seems that they were not

cue0148663
00:53:19.780 --> 00:53:21.780
originally from that, but they had come

cue0148664
00:53:21.780 --> 00:53:23.780
from ʾAshkenazim and so on. Now.

cue0148665
00:53:23.780 --> 00:53:25.780
His father,

cue0148666
00:53:25.780 --> 00:53:27.780
he dealt with Paltry.

cue0148667
00:53:27.780 --> 00:53:29.780
But because

cue0148668
00:53:29.780 --> 00:53:31.780
Izmir, it's on the

cue0148669
00:53:31.780 --> 00:53:33.780
Izmir is a beautiful town, you should go.

cue0148670
00:53:33.780 --> 00:53:35.780
It's very nice. I mean, I was

cue0148671
00:53:35.780 --> 00:53:37.780
in Izmir many times. It's a beautiful

cue0148672
00:53:37.780 --> 00:53:39.780
old Jewish community.

cue0148673
00:53:39.780 --> 00:53:41.780
And Izmir is by the

cue0148674
00:53:41.780 --> 00:53:43.780
harbor. And therefore,

cue0148675
00:53:43.780 --> 00:53:45.780
there were many agents.

cue0148676
00:53:45.780 --> 00:53:47.780
Dutch agents,

cue0148677
00:53:47.780 --> 00:53:49.780
British agents,

cue0148678
00:53:49.780 --> 00:53:51.780
and French agents

cue0148679
00:53:51.780 --> 00:53:53.780
who they had merchandise, and they

cue0148680
00:53:53.780 --> 00:53:55.780
wanted some Jews, they needed always Jews,

cue0148681
00:53:55.780 --> 00:53:57.780
because only you could trust the Jews,

cue0148682
00:53:57.780 --> 00:53:59.780
to serve as a representative

cue0148683
00:53:59.780 --> 00:54:01.780
in Izmir. Either to

cue0148684
00:54:01.780 --> 00:54:03.780
receive the merchandise that they sent

cue0148685
00:54:03.780 --> 00:54:05.780
from Europe, or to send the payment

cue0148686
00:54:05.780 --> 00:54:07.780
and so on. The father of Shabbet

cue0148687
00:54:07.780 --> 00:54:09.780
Taizeri became

cue0148688
00:54:09.780 --> 00:54:11.780
an agent for Dutch

cue0148689
00:54:11.780 --> 00:54:13.780
and English merchants.

cue0148690
00:54:13.780 --> 00:54:15.780
And in a short time,

cue0148691
00:54:15.780 --> 00:54:17.780
he becomes a wealthy man.

cue0148692
00:54:17.780 --> 00:54:19.780
As a matter of fact, the two

cue0148693
00:54:19.780 --> 00:54:21.780
brothers of Shabbet Taizeri

cue0148694
00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:23.780
were very, very wealthy.

cue0148695
00:54:23.780 --> 00:54:25.780
They were businessmen.

cue0148696
00:54:25.780 --> 00:54:27.780
Shabbet Taizeri, apparently,

cue0148697
00:54:27.780 --> 00:54:29.780
everybody says two things

cue0148698
00:54:29.780 --> 00:54:31.780
about Shabbet Taizeri, even his great enemies.

cue0148699
00:54:31.780 --> 00:54:33.780
They say, he was a

cue0148700
00:54:33.780 --> 00:54:35.780
genius, a very intelligent person.

cue0148701
00:54:35.780 --> 00:54:37.780
And he studied with two

cue0148702
00:54:37.780 --> 00:54:39.780
great Ḥakhamim. One of them

cue0148703
00:54:39.780 --> 00:54:41.780
was Isaac the Alba, and the

cue0148704
00:54:41.780 --> 00:54:43.780
other, Yoseph Eskava.

cue0148705
00:54:43.780 --> 00:54:45.780
The name Eskava is familiar to us.

cue0148706
00:54:45.780 --> 00:54:47.780
Yoseph Eskava was the Rabbi Rashid,

cue0148707
00:54:47.780 --> 00:54:49.780
the chief Rabbi of Izmir.

cue0148708
00:54:49.780 --> 00:54:51.780
The second thing that they say about

cue0148709
00:54:51.780 --> 00:54:53.780
Shabbet Taizeri,

cue0148710
00:54:53.780 --> 00:54:55.780
everybody says, that not

cue0148711
00:54:55.780 --> 00:54:57.780
only he was a great

cue0148712
00:54:57.780 --> 00:54:59.780
genius, but he had the most

cue0148713
00:54:59.780 --> 00:55:01.780
charming, enchanting personality.

cue0148714
00:55:01.780 --> 00:55:03.780
Apparently, he was

cue0148715
00:55:03.780 --> 00:55:05.780
given charisma.

cue0148716
00:55:05.780 --> 00:55:07.780
He had, also to say,

cue0148717
00:55:07.780 --> 00:55:09.780
the sweetest of all boys. He must have been

cue0148718
00:55:09.780 --> 00:55:11.780
a great Ḥazzan. And

cue0148719
00:55:11.780 --> 00:55:13.780
he got the Semicha

cue0148720
00:55:13.780 --> 00:55:15.780
at the age of 15.

cue0148721
00:55:15.780 --> 00:55:17.780
So it shows that the man, apparently,

cue0148722
00:55:17.780 --> 00:55:19.780
when he was a young person,

cue0148723
00:55:19.780 --> 00:55:21.780
he was a very studious

cue0148724
00:55:21.780 --> 00:55:23.780
and very serious

cue0148725
00:55:23.780 --> 00:55:25.780
individual. But as soon as

cue0148726
00:55:25.780 --> 00:55:27.780
he got the Semicha,

cue0148727
00:55:27.780 --> 00:55:29.780
he retires from public

cue0148728
00:55:29.780 --> 00:55:31.780
life. And he

cue0148729
00:55:31.780 --> 00:55:33.780
started studying qabbala

cue0148730
00:55:33.780 --> 00:55:35.780
on his own.

cue0148731
00:55:35.780 --> 00:55:37.780
Now, I am prejudiced.

cue0148732
00:55:37.780 --> 00:55:39.780
I'm going to tell you I'm prejudiced.

cue0148733
00:55:39.780 --> 00:55:41.780
Parenthesis.

cue0148734
00:55:41.780 --> 00:55:43.780
Of course, my prejudice

cue0148735
00:55:43.780 --> 00:55:45.780
is also the effect of Shabbat Taizeri.

cue0148736
00:55:45.780 --> 00:55:47.780
Because in our tradition,

cue0148737
00:55:47.780 --> 00:55:49.780
they tell us two things about qabbala.

cue0148738
00:55:49.780 --> 00:55:51.780
I know today people don't listen to me,

cue0148739
00:55:51.780 --> 00:55:53.780
but there are two very important things about qabbala.

cue0148740
00:55:53.780 --> 00:55:55.780
Number one, they tell you

cue0148741
00:55:55.780 --> 00:55:57.780
never study qabbala on your own.

cue0148742
00:55:57.780 --> 00:55:59.780
That's number one.

cue0148743
00:55:59.780 --> 00:56:01.780
No matter who you are,

